P1-2  sql/setup_likes.sql:18-19
      "Users can view all likes" USING (true) — anyone sees who liked what.
      Fix: SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id). Counts stay on songs.like_count.

P1-3  sql/setup_likes.sql increment/decrement_like_count
      No auth, not SECURITY DEFINER. Anon key can forge trending.
      like_service.dart insert then separate RPC = desync (insert ok, increment fail).
      Upsert alone does NOT fix counts.
      Fix: one SECURITY DEFINER toggle_like(uuid) that inserts/deletes likes AND
      updates like_count. REVOKE ALL FROM PUBLIC; GRANT EXECUTE TO authenticated.
      Same pattern for increment_play_count (throttle or stop exposing to client).

P1-4  SQL for songs, singers, favorites, profiles, singers_with_song_count,
      increment_play_count is NOT IN THE REPO.
      If RLS is off → anyone with the leaked key can DELETE/UPDATE songs.
      If RLS on with no policies → app shows no data.
      Fix: add sql/setup_all.sql:
        songs/singers: RLS on, SELECT public, no client writes
        favorites: RLS, CRUD only where auth.uid() = user_id
        profiles: RLS, select/insert own row; do NOT allow client to
        UPDATE subscription_status
      Policies must be re-runnable (DROP IF EXISTS).

